title: 'Decide: what should a start do when prompts/list or resources/list gets no
  answer?'
updated: 2026-11-06T14:41:30Z
---

From k130. Since k130 a refresh that gets no answer to prompts/list or resources/list fails and keeps the manifest; a start still takes no answer for an empty list, stores it over a good cache and notifies listeners. Options: (1) leave the start lenient (current): no call fails because of a list, the next refresh repairs it; (2) make the start strict: the call fails and counts toward the crash loop, so a slow prompts/list makes the tools unusable too; (3) on no answer during a start, keep the cached prompts/resources: the cache stays good, at the price of possibly stale lists and a little more code. Maintainer call.
